-- title:
--   Dual of a Vélu 2-isogeny: double quotient equals doubling
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field in which $2 \neq 0$, and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $K$ with invertible discriminant. Let $x_0, y_0 \in K$ satisfy the affine Weierstrass equation of $W$ and $W.\mathrm{veluGy}(x_0,y_0) = -(2y_0 + a_1 x_0 + a_3) = 0$, and suppose the discriminant of $W' := W.\mathrm{veluQuotient2}\,x_0\,y_0$ — the curve with the same $a_1,a_2,a_3$ and with $a_4$ replaced by $a_4 - 5g$ and $a_6$ by $a_6 - b_2 g - 7 x_0 g$, where $g = W.\mathrm{veluGx}(x_0,y_0) = 3x_0^2 + 2a_2x_0 + a_4 - a_1y_0$ — is nonzero. The assertion is that there are $x_1, y_1 \in K$ satisfying the affine equation of $W'$ with $W'.\mathrm{veluGy}(x_1,y_1) = 0$, such that $W'' := W'.\mathrm{veluQuotient2}\,x_1\,y_1$ has nonzero discriminant, together with a Weierstrass variable change $C$ with $C \bullet W = W''$, for which: (i) every pair $(x,y)$ on $W$ with $\mathrm{veluGy}(x,y)=0$ and $x \neq x_0$ has $\mathrm{velu2X}\,x_0\,y_0\,x = x + g/(x-x_0) = x_1$ and $\mathrm{velu2Y}\,x_0\,y_0\,x\,y = y - g\,(a_1(x-x_0)+y-y_0)/(x-x_0)^2 = y_1$; and (ii) for every point $P$ of the affine group of $W$, transporting $\mathrm{veluPointMap2}$ applied twice (first for $W$ at $(x_0,y_0)$, then for $W'$ at $(x_1,y_1)$) back along the bijection $W''(K) \simeq W(K)$ induced by $C$ gives $2P$.
--
--   This is the explicit form, in Vélu's coordinates, of the statement that a $2$-isogeny composed with its dual is multiplication by $2$: the dual's kernel is generated by the image $(x_1,y_1)$ of the $2$-torsion of $W$, and quotienting $W'$ by it returns $W$ up to a change of Weierstrass coordinates. It is used in the construction of the rational $2$-isogeny and of its composite description, and in the corresponding statement for quotients by full kernels.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_exists_variableChange_eq_veluQuotient2_veluQuotient2_comp_eq_two_smul_of_two_ne_zero.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_WeierstrassCurve_VeluPointMap2
